 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No idols drawn. 35:13-25 is one chip, so «لا يهدي إلا أن يهدى» stays whole. Light for «الله يهدي للحق» (allowed at His name), wind for «ظنا». 36:6-12 is not glossed (Al-Muyassar's «لا يغني» repeats the verse). STAGING v4: c1 (35) stays ambient: it is entirely the Prophet's commanded words to the idolaters about who guides (no idol drawn, nobody shown); the background stays quiet over the whole verse; a geometric plate starts on His guiding (35:11). c2 (36) is staged in a town by day: one small group of three idolaters (dark robes, countable; the tafsirs say nothing about the rest of them, so no second group is drawn) turns its back on 36:5 under a wind plate (they follow only conjecture) and shakes its head on 36:9 (conjecture avails nothing against the truth; As-Sa'di: they held it to be true); no idol, statue or worship is drawn and nobody faces an empty side; the camera closes on them on 36:16 while His knowledge of what they do is recited (quiet over 36:13-17). The cover now shows the geometric plate on His guiding (35:12)."
 },
